  """
// Neutrino Forced Chirality (02b §8.1).
// Neutrinos are the ONLY particle with structurally forced chirality.
// Only left-handed neutrinos exist.
//
// Neutrinos traverse the SU(2)-complex through space as they
// propagate. Their chirality closes over the triangle through
// spatial propagation:
//   XY leg: electron neutrino flavor
//   YZ leg: muon neutrino flavor
//   ZX leg: tau neutrino flavor
//   Total: complete chiral closure (spin-1/2 satisfied)
//
// The Higgs defines "forward" around the SU(2)-complex via its
// 3-tick self-interference. Right-handed neutrinos would have to
// traverse the complex backward. This is structurally impossible,
// not merely energetically unfavorable.
//
// Consequences:
//   Three flavors: three legs of triangle.
//   Oscillation: spatial propagation = loop propagation.
//   Tiny mass: chirality spread over 3 steps, not localized.
//   Left-handed only: forward is defined by the Higgs.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.chirality, theory.physics.higgs,
//               theory.coherence.law1
  """
